    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 14).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, **1,783 of 32,253 Symbol nodes (5.5%) are orphans** — they have zero edges (no inbound, no outbound). Breakdown by kind:\n\n| Kind | Orphan count | Likely-legitimate? |\n|---|---:|---|\n| variable | 1301 | partial — many module-level constants may not need outbound edges, but inbound (used-by) should exist |\n| **function** | **113** | **NO — actionable** |\n| call_site | 111 | unclear semantics; needs investigation |\n| external_symbol | 106 | possibly OK (synthetic boundaries) |\n| dependency | 67 | possibly OK (declared deps that aren't actually used in code) |\n| module | 44 | likely related to R14-B (module-kind orphans) |\n| export | 18 | should have inbound from importers; orphan = broken |\n| **class** | **13** | **NO — actionable** |\n| project | 7 | likely OK (workspace-level metadata nodes) |\n| file | 3 | likely related to R14-B |\n\n**Actionable subset: 113 orphan functions + 13 orphan classes.** These are the highest-confidence \"this is a real bug\" signal — a function or class definition with zero edges means the static graph thinks nothing calls it, nothing instantiates it, nothing imports it, nothing contains it. For an in-repo definition, that's almost always wrong.\n\n**Why this matters.**\n\n1. **Orphan functions + classes are likely the same family as INV-mofav** (Python analyzer drops nested function definitions). If a class method has a nested helper, the helper might exist as a Symbol but have no inbound edge because nobody captured the calls. The 113+13 actionable orphans need triage to distinguish:\n   - (a) Nested functions/classes whose call sites weren't captured (INV-mofav family)\n   - (b) Class methods called through polymorphic dispatch (WI-vuton family)\n   - (c) Genuinely dead code (the value-add of the audit)\n\n2. **18 orphan exports** are interesting. An `export` kind suggests `__all__` entries or explicit re-exports. They should have at least one inbound `module_exports` edge. Orphan = the export-detection isn't connecting to the exported symbol.\n\n3. **1301 orphan variables** is the largest group but the hardest to assess without per-language conventions. Module-level constants that are only READ (no writes) might legitimately be edge-less in a call-graph view. Module-level constants that are WRITTEN by external code (e.g., monkey-patched test fixtures) should have inbound `references` edges.\n\n**Severity.** Medium for the actionable 126 (113 functions + 13 classes); low for the variables/sentinels.\n\n**Fix proposal — investigation-first.**\n\n1. **Triage the 113 orphan functions and 13 orphan classes.** Sample 10 of each. For each:\n   - Manually verify whether they have any caller / instantiation / import in the source\n   - Classify: actual dead code, nested-function (INV-mofav), polymorphic dispatch (WI-vuton), framework lifecycle (WI-vuton), or other\n\n2. **Based on the triage, file follow-up items** for each root cause. Most are likely INV-mofav or WI-vuton facets, in which case this audit is a cross-validation signal rather than a new bug.\n\n3. **Add a sentinel test on the self-analysis fixture.** Once the underlying causes are addressed, the orphan-function count should drop dramatically. A test asserting `orphan_function_count < N` (with N chosen from a fresh post-fix baseline) catches regressions.\n\n**Test gap.** No current property test for orphan-node thresholds. Add one after triage establishes a healthy baseline.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `INV-mofav-...` (filed round 10) — Python analyzer's nested-function blindness; likely covers a portion of the 113 orphan functions\n- `WI-vuton-...` (filed round 11) — dead-code-maybe polymorphic dispatch FPs; likely covers another portion\n- `R14-A (INV-...)` — file-kind nodes with broken span; 3 of the orphan files may be related\n- `R14-B (INV-...)` — module-kind orphan; 44 orphan modules are within this scope\n- `INV-tisid-...` (filed round 11) — supply chain test-file misclassification; orthogonal but related \"graph correctness\" audit"  # bf80
    fields: {}  # bf80
